OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786940279
OL,3,CMet Police accused of failing in legal
OL,4,Cduty to Al Fayed trafficking victims
OL,6,FShe received a positive conclusive
OL,7,Fgrounds decision that she was a victim
OL,8,Fof human trafficking in July.
OL,10,FThe Met have been "reactive as opposed
OL,11,Fto proactive" throughout the whole
OL,12,Finvestigation, Margo said.
OL,14,FIsabella, also a pseudonym, worked in
OL,15,Fthe chairman's office at Harrods in
OL,16,F2001, where she was trafficked. She
OL,17,Falso reported her experience to the
OL,18,Fpolice in 2024.
OL,26,@rD@SOUsD@MO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/24
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30812
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786940279
OL,3,CMet Police accused of failing in legal
OL,4,Cduty to Al Fayed trafficking victims
OL,6,FThe Met have not offered her a
OL,7,Freferral to the NRM, despite telling
OL,8,Fher in 2025 that her circumstances
OL,9,Ffell under the definition of
OL,10,Ftrafficking.
OL,12,FAfter self-initiating a NRM referral
OL,13,Fthrough Unseen, Isabella received a
OL,14,Fconclusive grounds decision from the
OL,15,FHome Office in May, identifying her as
OL,16,Fa victim of trafficking.
OL,18,FReflecting on the fact the Met are now
OL,19,Fcontacting survivors about referring
OL,20,Fthem to the NRM, she said: "I think
OL,21,Fthe sequence matters.
OL,26,@|D@\OU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G12/24
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30813
SC,0013
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786940279
OL,3,CMet Police accused of failing in legal
OL,4,Cduty to Al Fayed trafficking victims
OL,6,F"Survivors had to force the state to
OL,7,Frecognise trafficking in a case the
OL,8,FMet now says had trafficking always at
OL,9,Fits heart.
OL,11,F"Referring suspected victims to the
OL,12,FNRM is a statutory duty, it's not
OL,13,Foptional. That duty is triggered the
OL,14,Fmoment that trafficking is suspected,
OL,15,Fnot when it's proved...
OL,17,F"The legal duty is that it should be
OL,18,Fmade promptly, and the threshold is
OL,19,Flow: reasonable grounds to suspect, no
OL,20,Fdefinitive proof needed."
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@AOUyD@AOU|D@YO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G13/24
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
